  "reasoning": "The claim was denied with CO-97 (bundled service), which is a final adjudication indicating the service is not separately payable under the payer's rules. Resubmitting the same claim would violate the duplicate claim rule (CO-18), and an appeal is unlikely to succeed against a standard bundling denial without new clinical evidence that the payer has not yet considered. Given the high success rate of billing the patient in similar past cases and the fact that the patient is responsible for the full allowed amount due to the deductible, billing the patient is the most effective next step to collect the funds.",
